[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3299716493","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110436#issuecomment-3299716493","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110436","id":3299716493,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Era2N","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-16T17:33:59Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T17:33:59Z","body":"I get similar results on an M2 Macbook. \n_First plane +lights; second lights + mesh tiles; third mesh tiles, no lights_\n<img width=\"295\" height=\"184\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d9b39b4b-a1e7-4588-b760-b8516367db1a\" />\n\nI am not willing to call this a performance bug. This is an interesting MRP that could be used to help improve performance. But it is such an extreme edge case. There are 6562 dynamic meshes all moving every single frame _and_ they are all within range of 729 lights. It is not a realistic scenario at all and is totally contrived to stress test this aspect of the engine. \n\nThat being said, I do think we can improve this situation a lot and the MRP will help us identify low hanging fruits in both our code to update object transforms in the rendering server and our code to pair objects with lights in the rendering server. So I do think this report is useful. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3299716493/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3299877642","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110436#issuecomment-3299877642","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110436","id":3299877642,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7EsCMK","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-16T18:25:43Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T18:25:43Z","body":"Eh, this is nothing, You don't want to see what my Game is doing 😆 \n\nAlso I just checked something, this must be a bug, changing the tile material to be unshaded, or setting all the light cull masks to not include the 1st layer that the meshes are all exclusively in doesn't change the performance basically at all.\n\nThis is also probably why I've noticed the issue in my game, as for some stats with my game are as follows:\n\n1) Some 200 Space Ships, each with a couple to a couple dozen lights (spot lights) depending on the type\n2) 0 to about 700 Asteroids in the level\n3) In intense combat, I can typically see some 6 Thousand bullets & impacts (sometimes even more), each Being unshaded GPU Particles (or billboard mesh instance quads for bullets) and each one of these effects has an unshadowed Light (360 deg omni light imitation for impacts, omni lights for bullets)\n4) Typical meshes are 20-50k triangles\n5) Clustered Element limit was set to 8192 because in some edge cases with lower values like 4096 I've actually seen lights not existing, and that's with the spot-omni trick that I'm using to have an increased light count budget\n\nFrankly I find it absolutely bonkers that my GPU, the RX 6600 is doing this at Native 1440p and only taking some 6ms (with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/55289, without it's about 7.5ms per typical frame, with all of the above going on) and Honestly when I first decided to try adding lights to everything I expected my GPU to be Screaming in Agony from all the lights, not my CPU.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3299877642/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3299936836","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110436#issuecomment-3299936836","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110436","id":3299936836,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7EsQpE","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-16T18:45:20Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T18:46:39Z","body":"Additional Note, I just tested and MultiMeshInstances can be used as an optimization strategy\n\nthe tiles have been replaced with roughly a similar tile count but as a MultiMeshInstance and it's looking much like just the plane rendering now\n<img width=\"84\" height=\"151\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2142b2d1-26f2-49df-89c8-a9037d7c751c\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3299936836/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3299941951","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110436#issuecomment-3299941951","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110436","id":3299941951,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7EsR4_","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-16T18:47:02Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T18:47:02Z","body":"> Also I just checked something, this must be a bug, changing the tile material to be unshaded, or setting all the light cull masks to not include the 1st layer that the meshes are all exclusively in doesn't change the performance basically at all.\n\nThe cost likely comes from 2 things:\n1. Updating the transform in the rendering server. That has to happen regardless of the material or cull masks\n2. Pairing the lights with the objects. The expensive part here is doing overlap checks and checking the mask etc. So while the light may not end up pairing with the object (due to being unshaded, or culled), the check still needs to be done. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3299941951/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3299944629","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110436#issuecomment-3299944629","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110436","id":3299944629,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7EsSi1","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-16T18:47:55Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T18:48:04Z","body":"> Additional Note, I just tested and MultiMeshInstances can be used as an optimization strategy\n> \n> the tiles have been replaced with roughly a similar tile count but as a MultiMeshInstance and it's looking much like just the plane rendering now <img alt=\"Image\" width=\"84\" height=\"151\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/50302479/490198865-2142b2d1-26f2-49df-89c8-a9037d7c751c.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..P21pVGsd-M0OY32xp3AK1zTkQWH2pnybfs8qxQXOJy0\">\n\nThat's totally expected. You went from 6562 objects to just a single one. So it should be close to 6000 times faster...","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3299944629/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3299951981","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110436#issuecomment-3299951981","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110436","id":3299951981,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7EsUVt","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-16T18:50:43Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T18:59:17Z","body":"Yeah I expected the result too once it occurred to me to try it, and that is what I'll base my game Optimization around, though that will eliminate any frustum culling effectively (which TBH not a big deal) I just don't know if ALODs work properly with MMI which is the bigger concern for me, but I guess I'll have to find out\n\nEdit: Well I guess even without ALOD I'm fine GPU wise, with a full scene without ALOD being some 10ms from 6ms, and going from 30 fps with 80% of the cost being Drawing to a locked 60 is totally worth it, just must make sure to keep this game away from TI at All costs 🤣 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3299951981/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3299982671","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110436#issuecomment-3299982671","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110436","id":3299982671,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Esb1P","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-16T19:01:16Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T19:02:54Z","body":"> Yeah I expected the result too once it occurred to me to try it, and that is what I'll base my game Optimization around, though that will eliminate any frustum culling effectively (which TBH not a big deal) I just don't know if ALODs work properly with MMI which is the bigger concern for me, but I guess I'll have to find out\n\nDon't do just one chunk. Split your scene into a few dozen chunks, then you will get the benefit of ALODs _and_ decent frustum culling. Even better, avoid updating your transforms every single frame, that will significantly cut down on your frame time as well. \n\nThere is a reason that, in AAA games, 99% of geometry is totally static and local light shadows are almost always pre-baked. Dynamic local lighting should be used sparingly and dynamic objects should be limited to only those that actually need to move\n\n_Edit: I just tested with full lights and full meshes, but with the transforms disabled and the cost was only cut in half. I expected to it to be much closer to the single quad case. So there is definitely a bunch of unnecessary overhead. I bet we can cut the overall CPU cost of this MRP in half!_","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3299982671/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300010282","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110436#issuecomment-3300010282","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110436","id":3300010282,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Esikq","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-16T19:10:22Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T19:10:22Z","body":"sadly my game is entirely dynamic, and the entire level can be seen at the edge of the map, and all the lights are tied to dynamic objects, so most of the typical optimization ideas that would work for most other games don't here.\n\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/performance/using_multimesh.html doesn't specify if MMI has ALOD and to what extent, but eh, even if the entire scene is always rendered and at full detail I guess I can get away with it if I really have to.\n\nI mean do keep in mind the RX 6600 is supposed to be a 1080p card, not a 1440p one.. I'd just be bringing the performance closer to the expected GPU screaming scenario and still not anywhere near as bad as I expected for it (I expected 30 fps 1080p due to GPU bottlenecks, not 1440p with 30 fps that could be 60 without a breaking a sweat, due to the CPU getting murdered)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300010282/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300056844","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110436#issuecomment-3300056844","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110436","id":3300056844,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Est8M","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-16T19:24:59Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T19:24:59Z","body":"> https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/performance/using_multimesh.html doesn't specify if MMI has ALOD and to what extent, but eh, even if the entire scene is always rendered and at full detail I guess I can get away with it if I really have to.\n\nALOD is a property of the mesh, not the MeshInstance/MultiMeshInstance. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300056844/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300063073","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110436#issuecomment-3300063073","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110436","id":3300063073,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Esvdh","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-16T19:26:46Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T19:28:40Z","body":"ah good so I'm not going to lose out on that, that's fantastic. \nMaybe TI won't kill me as much for just ditching Frustum Culling 🤣 \n\nP.S. I can also possibly make my own Frustum Culling logic as part of the MMI render setup","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300063073/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300117453","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110436#issuecomment-3300117453","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110436","id":3300117453,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Es8vN","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https:/